{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Generation.</b> Because everything found under the sun is composed of four elements from which they emerged and to which they return—and they are fire, wind, which is air, and water and earth—he mentioned all four, and began with earth, for it is like a mother, and afterward he mentioned the sun, the place of fire, because of its great heat, and it is the generating fire, and afterward wind and water. And he said of the earth that all who are formed from it return to it, as in the matter of 'for dust you are and to dust you shall return.' And it stands, while a generation comes and a generation goes. It is possible that the meaning of דור is like strangers, and similarly מדור באהלי רשע."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved מורכב as 'composed'; היולדת read as 'a mother' (lit. 'the one who gives birth'); quoted verse כי עפר אתה ואל עפר תשוב identified as Genesis 3:19; מדור באהלי רשע cited without book name, likely Job 18:15."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:49.737563905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}